From 29bf2a60e97f5942b483e475c52e1c8bbe9870f7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jakub Jirutka <jakub@jirutka.cz>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 23:31:59 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] feat: add native syslog logging support

Add `syslog` as a supported log format alongside `console` and `json`,
using Go's standard log/syslog package.

Map slog levels to syslog priorities and omit redundant timestamps and
severity fields, which are already provided by syslog.

Format log entries as a plain message followed by optional key=value
attributes, rather than using slog.TextHandler's msg="<message>" format.
This requires a custom slog handler to preserve structured attributes,
groups, and proper quoting without parsing or rewriting formatted output.

Normalize embedded newlines to keep each syslog entry on a single line.

The existing logging formats and default behavior remain unchanged.

Signed-off-by: Jakub Jirutka <jakub@jirutka.cz>
